nodecode-brownout is a rewrite of Osiyomeoh's Osiyomeoh/brownout:

  https://github.com/Osiyomeoh/brownout
  commit 6d983d5da32c6cdd6a3551426de87d44a78dbfea
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Samuel Aleonomoh (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole of core/policy.py and core/forecast.py -- the four
states, the tick that decides what a reading means, the keep that cancels an
automatic park, and the runway measured tick to tick from the percent drops
rather than fitted to a flat plateau; core/power.py -- the pmset, sysfs and
NUT/upsc readers, parsed as text and answering no reading rather than a
guess; the watcher thread and the file lock of __init__.py, here one
nodecode worker; the pre_tool_call guard that holds tool calls while parked;
and /brownout's status, park, keep, resume, test-alert and replay verbs.

Left out, and why: the Hermes-specific surfaces have no Nodecode
counterpart. `hermes send --to <target>' (a message through the gateway's
chat credentials) became a standing notice under the cell's key: every
shell shows it and the agent reads it in the notices block of its next
request, so the same fact reaches the same two readers with no credential
and no network of its own. Pausing scheduled cron jobs became the tool-call
hold alone, because a cron job here is another cell's business and a park
that reached into it would be a dependency; a cron turn is held at its first
tool call instead. The per-home file lock, the atomically replaced
state.json and the commands.jsonl relay existed so several Hermes processes
on one home agree on one watcher; a Nodecode cell starts once in the one
process that serves the home, so the worker and its state are that
process's. The outbox that retried an undelivered message for an hour is
gone with the network: a notice cannot fail. events.jsonl became the last
five things said, which /brownout status shows. The section gains
allow_when_parked (tools that still run while parked) and the reading
trace replay reads a neutral JSONL of {t, on_ac, pct} instead of raw pmset
output, so a trace recorded on one platform replays on another.
